    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive anchor. With an elite efficiency score of 82.13, he occupies the lead-off spot against Merrill Kelly, whose 5.27 xERA creates a target-rich environment. The combination of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s elite speed\u2014our scarcest commodity\u2014and the favorable platoon split against Kelly makes him our highest-upside play. **Junior Caminero** also projects as a high-impact starter (72.50) despite the left-handed matchup against Framber Valdez; his position in the three-hole and a favorable park adjustment keep his floor high enough to command the Utility spot.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 35.75 score. While **Dillon Dingler** benefits from park factors, his negative platoon adjustment against Rasmussen and a sub-40 efficiency rating dictated a benching to preserve our game caps. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** secured a strong 60.62 start, buoyed significantly by a +11% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against Kevin Gausman. We are closely monitoring the status of **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**; both are battling difficult matchups against Logan Gilbert (3.46 xERA), which has suppressed their efficiency scores into the marginal range (51.35 and 50.87, respectively). While the Zebras remain thin due to scheduled off-days for **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**, we are confident in the high-leverage spots provided by **Caleb Durbin** and **Pedro Ramirez** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
